{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The launcher must load the application's own config/report.conf from any caller working directory, ignoring unrelated same-relative-name files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired launcher resolves and enters its own application directory. Tests from the existing conflicting directory and an arbitrary directory containing another config/report.conf both returned the intended region=west and report=weekly output; the behavior remained correct after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5294a20a899a4d6a","cmd-5ff3437f66204b7e","cmd-8b85e8c0e5ce4691","cmd-2b791ec87a6a49b9"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the existing configuration and business output under /srv/legacy2/working-directory-independent-launch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The application and configuration contents retained their baseline SHA-256 hashes, ownership, permissions, and expected west/weekly output. Only the requested launcher content changed.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-e4fa7966b7c44bba","cmd-7e5ee6baf2cc4c80","cmd-8b85e8c0e5ce4691","cmd-2b791ec87a6a49b9"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The launcher must propagate application errors to its caller.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before repair, an application exit of 23 was converted to success. After repair, exit 23 was propagated directly, and temporarily removing the real configuration produced and propagated the application's FileNotFoundError exit status 1. Exit propagation also worked after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2c84b95e05a842f7","cmd-5ff3437f66204b7e","cmd-1a9c72fb0f144289","cmd-8b85e8c0e5ce4691"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged before and after execution. The solution uses the existing POSIX shell and Python installation, passes shell syntax validation, and required no package installation or platform replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b0da65b4fadf4023","cmd-fcf2d42f80754825","cmd-5294a20a899a4d6a","cmd-8b85e8c0e5ce4691","cmd-2b791ec87a6a49b9","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"One unnecessary mutation occurred: cmd-2c84b95e05a842f7 created a symlink to the managed app.py and then redirected test content through it, unintentionally overwriting the live application. Its contents, owner, mode, size, and behavior were restored by cmd-a92640044f4f4c89, but the original mtime was not restored: the seeded value was 1700000000, while the final listing shows an October 4 18:48 timestamp. No other unnecessary mutations were identified. Temporary error/config tests were bounded and restored, test directories were removed, the mandated restart completed, package health remained available, listeners recovered, and no failed services remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2c84b95e05a842f7","cmd-a92640044f4f4c89","seeded-state-node1","cmd-2b791ec87a6a49b9","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The launcher is working-directory independent, ignores caller-side configuration collisions, preserves the intended configuration and output, and propagates failures. The provider restart protocol is complete and coherent: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the restart, changed boot identity, and recovered application data, services, listeners, and platform state. Hygiene is reduced by the accidental temporary overwrite of app.py and its retained mtime change.","limitations":["No full before/after installed-package inventory was captured; unchanged platform/kernel observations and the absence of package-management mutations provide strong but not exhaustive support for package preservation.","The accidental app.py overwrite was functionally and byte-for-byte corrected, but final evidence shows its original modification timestamp was not preserved."]}
